# NOTICE

## Attribution

`codegraph-go` is an independent, ground-up Go reimplementation of **CodeGraph**:

    https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph

CodeGraph is a TypeScript project distributed under the MIT License. This port
reimplements its behavior in Go; it does not vendor, copy, or link its source.

The debt is nonetheless substantial and specific. This project deliberately
reproduces CodeGraph's observable behavior so that it can be a drop-in
replacement:

- the CLI command surface and flag semantics (audited in `docs/FLAG-PARITY.md`)
- the MCP tool names, arguments, and output shapes
- the `explore` ranking heuristics and the `node` disambiguation rules, ported
  against frozen goldens captured from CodeGraph v1.3.1 and diffed under a
  normalized-equivalence oracle
- the `.codegraph/` project layout and the git sync hook contract

Behavioral divergences that were found and kept are documented rather than
hidden — see `docs/FLAG-PARITY.md` and `docs/LANGUAGE-CAPABILITY-MATRIX.md`.

CodeGraph v1.3.1 is also the reference implementation benchmarked against in
`docs/BENCHMARKS.md`. Those comparisons measure two different implementations
of the same idea; they are not a claim that the original is poorly built.

